codemap 9
tour comment-model
kind data
author ai
group map
note A comment is a note the human leaves for the agent on a tour, a step or lines of code; this is its model. Comments are not part of the Map: they live in their own collection, are read and written by io-comments outside .codemap/, and nothing in the map refers to them. A comment's place is a CommentTarget: a tour by name, a step by tour name and step id, or an Anchor pinned exactly like a step's, so a code comment follows its symbol when code moves above it and goes stale when its lines change. Its state is open until a reply arrives, answered after; deleting it (dismiss or withdraw in the window) removes it from the collection. Every place is kept by name, so renaming a tour or moving a file leaves the comment where nothing matches; the GUI and the CLI show that as gone rather than guessing.

